#: 441659be521a4e489a95937b146318c5
msgid "To get signals to ESCs or servos you need to use a UART. The default setup is to send 4 PWM signals as serial data on **/dev/tty-3**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-qualcomm-snapdragon-flight-kit.rst:352
#: be8013765e034b79abe0a111cb046976
msgid "`This firmware <https://github.com/tridge/ardupilot/tree/hal-qurt/libraries/RC_Channel/examples/RC_UART>`__ will read the UART serial stream and output to the PWM output of the board you use. For example, you could use a Pixracer or Pixhawk board. It is designed to work with this firmware for any ArduPilot compatible board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-qualcomm-snapdragon-flight-kit.rst:360
#: c343518f57314f1990673c272128240f
msgid "`Qualcomm/Intrinsyc have released a ESC <https://shop.intrinsyc.com/products/qualcomm-electronic-speed-control-board>`__ for use with this board but it has not been tested for use with ArduPilot."
msgstr ""

